Start();
include(utilities);
include(unitTests);
registry(LookR);
define
    myLook pageFill="red";
    myBase inkColor="blue" boxFill="gray";
    ;
search LookR Utilities UnitTests list;
registry(RlT);
define
    pageFill;
    inkColor;
    lostOne;
    boxFill;
    req look:=myLook;
    sty2 fill:=boxFill;
    sty fill:=pageFill ink:=inkColor gone:=lostOne plain="x" width=4;
    ergoLook code={
        for grup in argument; attributes
            msHolds = *grup.isGrouP;
            if msHolds == 0;    continue;
            msData = **grup.datA;
            msList = **grup.listLengtH;
            msVia = **grup.isGrouP;
            if msData != 0 || msList != 0 || msVia != 0;    continue;
            msName := **grup.taG;
            if lkHas == 1 && *lkLook[*msName];
                msTo := *lkLook[*msName];
                *grup := **msTo;
            or lkBaseHas == 1 && *lkBase[*msName];
                msTo := *lkBase[*msName];
                *grup := **msTo;
            else
                msAttr = *grup.taG;
                cerr rlSays "REFUSING" argument.taG "-- its" msAttr "names the placeholder" msName "and no look holds it; name it in the request's look or in defaultLook":;
        };
    ;
search RlT LookR Utilities UnitTests list;
setLook(req);
print "lkHas" lkHas:;
lkBase := myBase;
lkBaseHas = 1;
rlSays = "probe:";
ergoLook(sty);
print "fill" sty.fill:;
print "ink" sty.ink:;
print "gone" sty.gone:;
print "plain" sty.plain:;
print "width" sty.width:;
lkBaseHas = 0;
lkHas = 0;
ergoLook(sty2);
print "neither boxFill" sty2.fill:;
cerr "RL SENTINEL":;
stop();

ergoSpecimen -- resolveLook (incant/utilities) rewritten with only the spellings docs/ergoCensus.md marks "works" on
incant/grammar (Clay's ergonomics census, 2026-11-19). incant/utilities is NOT changed; this file is the specimen.

WHAT IT USES
    continue in a for loop        replaces msPh, the "is this a placeholder" flag
    && and || in a condition      replace the nested ifs that were one condition
    if / or / else                replaces msDone, the "already resolved" flag, and its two re-tests
    (the for loop over argument's attributes, the holder reads, the := re-point and the refusal line are resolveLook's own)

LINES
    resolveLook as it stands        32 lines, 30 without its two comment lines; names msHolds msData msList msVia msPh msName msDone msTo msAttr (9)
    ergoLook, the rewrite           19 lines; msPh and msDone are gone (7 names)

HOW IT WAS CHECKED (2026-11-19, the bare build of 2026-11-18 14:10)
    The file above runs ergoLook. Replacing ergoLook with resolveLook in the two driver calls runs the original
    (it is in Utilities); the two outputs are byte-identical. The setup takes each arm once: fill resolves only through
    the request's look (the base has no pageFill), ink only through the base (the look has no inkColor), gone refuses by
    name, plain and width are skipped, and sty2's fill refuses with neither look on. A second run with lkHas = 0 in place
    of setLook(req) moves fill to a refusal, identically on both.
    ⚠ The looks live in their own registry (LookR) on purpose: an attribute named like a field in the same define writes
    that field (myBase's pageFill="green" set the placeholder pageFill itself), which made every run read "green".
    Not chased; recorded in the census report.
    ⚠ The printed values read as tag echoes (fill fill, ink ink) on both; which value a resolved attribute holds is not
    what this compares. The refusals are the arm witnesses.
